Let a frontend with no window play a replay file as the GUI's replay button does

A headless session could pause, resume, stop and change the speed of a replay, and follow it by replayStarted,
replaySpeedChanged and replayFinished, but it could not start one the way the GUI's replay button does: only a
script's loadReplay() starts a replay there, and that plays it as a script's, which says nothing in the main console
when it loads or ends. An app that offers the player a file of their own to play had no way to do it.

- THeadlessSession::playReplay(path) plays the replay file at that whole path in the session's profile through
  MudletReplay::load() without an error string, as mudlet::slot_replay() does, so localText says it is loading and
  when it is over, and replayStarted follows from the event loop.
- It is false, with the reason in errorString(), while a replay plays in any profile, for a file that cannot be read
  (with the system's reason) or is not a replay, while a script of the profile runs, and where submit() is refused.
- docs/headless.md says so beside pauseReplay().

Tested by Mudlet/android's native/tests/test_mudlet_engine.py (replay_playback: a recorded file played, its lines
shown, paused, resumed, faster and slower, stopped, played to its end; refused for a missing file, a file that is not
a replay and while one plays). The desktop is unchanged.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

